  "acceptedCodeReview": {
    "OPG-I2": {
      "id": "OPG-I2",
      "severity": "INFO",
      "text": "C2 'removing the guard recreates the foreign-value case' is evidenced by the real BASE RED (no capture, no guard, two reads; foreign-equal case only) rather than by a capture-without-guard mutant run. Static controls missing-type-gate/wrong-connective/widened-* plus reviewer RC02-RC04 cover guard removal/weakening at the AST layer. Acceptable; not an executed-mutant claim."
    },
    "OPG-L1": {
      "actualSourceImpact": "None for 746789a: reviewer P06 runs the selector on the HEAD tree itself (same 25 paths, 24 other blobs equal) and git name-status shows the only non-docs paths are dispatch.py and the test (outside the selector roots); P05 finds exactly one `.deliver` reference in the selector roots. The author's prepublication asserts (tracked == [dispatch], no untracked production) also covered it at WIP time.",
      "id": "OPG-L1",
      "minimalFix": "Before any reuse of finite_compatibility on source other than 746789a: derive the path set by running the selector on the evaluated tree (git grep on the target commit or an equivalent regex over its blobs) and compare with base_world(); keep 'modified-unrelated-module' as an injected control and add one tree-discovery control. No product or test change.",
      "observed": "current_world() reads the current bytes of base_world()'s 25 paths, so the path set passed to evaluate() always equals BASE's. SOURCE_WORLD_PATH_SET_CHANGED is therefore reachable only for a caller-injected synthetic world (control 'modified-unrelated-module'); a new selector-matching file in the evaluated tree (e.g. a second production deliver caller in a new module) would not be discovered by evaluate(current_world()). The claim 'source-set changes reject' holds for injected worlds, not for tree discovery.",
      "severity": "LOW",
      "source": "docs/vault/30_Development/Evidence/fleet5-b-a7-operation-guard-r1-20261107-codex/finite_compatibility.py lines 42-43 (current_world) with evaluate() line 186 (path-set check); blob 7b245536fbbf4f607a5dac0d75a1be4abd70e60c / sha256 e61b538446e0ba0b8b254874fadf9c820a3341a40dbf1ec51b63f95e32a105bf at 746789a",
      "status": "CARRIED_CONDITION_FOR_REUSE_NONBLOCKING_FOR_746789a"
    },
    "commit": "dc18f6681627aca9d3eceb7d5a85dbc97b551b5b",
    "verdict": "ACCEPT_NARROW_CODE_KEEP_HOLD",
